WEBVTT

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.711
<i>It seems today  </i>

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:04.587
<i>That all you see  </i>

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:08.133
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV  </i>

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:12.262
<i>  But where are those
good old-fashioned values  </i>

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:14.389
<i>On which we used to rely?  </i>

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:18.226
<i>Lucky there's a family guy  </i>

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:21.521
<i>  Lucky there's a man who
positively can do  </i>

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.106
<i>All the things that make us  </i>

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:24.441
<i>Laugh and cry  </i>

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:30.071
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!  </i>

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:32.741
{\an8}Hi, I'm Peter Griffin.

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:34.576
{\an8}It's almost Oscar night.

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:36.995
{\an8}Boy, we've lost so many greats this year,

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:38.955
{\an8}including a dead costume designer

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.540
{\an8}who will get spill-over applause

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.543
{\an8}from the photo of Sean Connery
that directly precedes him.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.463
{\an8}Tonight, we salute
some past Best Picture winners,

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:48.757
{\an8}whichever ones I spin on this wheel.

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:56.473
{\an8}The wheel has spoken!

00:00:56.473 --> 00:00:58.183
{\an8}<i>The Silence of the Lambs.</i>

00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:08.359
{\an8}Ah... what a beautiful day
to not get bodily fluids

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:10.361
{\an8}thrown in your face and hair.

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:14.657
{\an8}And now, for some rock tunes
to pump me up.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.077
{\an8}<i>One, two princes kneel before you...  </i>

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.413
{\an8}Oh, right, 'cause it's the early '90s.

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:22.332
{\an8}Vaulting over a log.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:24.084
{\an8}Jumping a water hazard.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.336
{\an8}Climbing up a cargo net.

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:28.379
{\an8}Becoming an FBI agent is basically

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:30.924
{\an8}like being on <i>Battle of the Network Stars.</i>

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.551
{\an8}<i>You rockets ain't in...  </i>

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:40.391
{\an8}- Aah!
- Agent Starling.

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:41.601
{\an8}Good to see you.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.353
{\an8}Wh-Why is your face so big?

00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:45.855
{\an8}Oh, this movie
is mostly extreme close-ups.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.816
{\an8}Oh. Yeah. Weird.

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:49.776
{\an8}Anyway, sorry you had to come so quickly,

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.153
{\an8}but this thing with no timetable
couldn't wait.

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:55.115
{\an8}We need you to talk
to a super smart psychopath.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.574
{\an8}How smart?

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:58.076
{\an8}Like, he can do
the <i>New York Times</i> crossword

00:01:58.076 --> 00:01:59.244
{\an8}through Thursday.

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:01.412
{\an8}Friday, he can maybe get a corner or two.

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:03.081
{\an8}So, what's the job?

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:04.666
{\an8}Fancy creep, eats people.

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:06.543
{\an8}- Talk to him.
- Got it.

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:08.461
{\an8}And this is a big deal,
'cause you're a woman.

00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:10.171
{\an8}We're not gonna say it's a big deal,

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:12.465
{\an8}but everyone watching
will know it's a big deal

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:13.758
{\an8}'cause of the time period,

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.343
{\an8}even though a man is helping you.

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:16.803
{\an8}Now run along, toots.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.269
{\an8}So, you're in the FBI, huh?

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:26.104
{\an8}Me too.

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:28.481
{\an8}Got this bad boy in Venice Beach.

00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:31.943
{\an8}Okay, all right.

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:33.653
{\an8}You can talk to Lecter now.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.495
{\an8}Hello, Clarice.

00:02:42.579 --> 00:02:44.831
{\an8}Dr. Lecter, I need your help.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.917
{\an8}Nope, nope, nope.
I'll only help if there's a quid pro quo.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.711
{\an8} Okay, what is it?

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:53.840
{\an8}I want Mario Lopez to record
my outgoing voice mail message.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.675
{\an8}What?! You're insane!

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:59.012
{\an8}He's a huge star
at this specific sliver of time.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.598
{\an8}Figure it out. Those are my terms.

00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:10.648
{\an8}Sorry, these Capri Suns
are notoriously difficult to open.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.737
{\an8}<i>Yeah, one, two...  </i>

00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:18.990
{\an8}: <i>That's what I said now  </i>

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.450
{\an8}<i>Princes...  </i>

00:03:27.498 --> 00:03:28.833
{\an8}You need some help?

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.084
{\an8}Yeah, thanks.

00:03:30.168 --> 00:03:33.504
{\an8}I can't seem to get
this giant 1991 computer

00:03:33.588 --> 00:03:35.673
{\an8}into the back of my van.

00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:39.594
{\an8}Careful, I had it on
for 20 minutes, so it's very hot.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:47.185
{\an8}Okay, I got what you asked for.

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:48.853
{\an8}<i>Hey, this is Mario Lopez</i>

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.355
{\an8}<i>letting you know that Hannibal Lecter</i>

00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:51.814
{\an8}<i>can't get to the phone right now,</i>

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.441
{\an8}<i>so please leave a message.</i>

00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:55.235
{\an8}<i>And now, I think
I'm about to be saved by the...</i>

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:57.570
Not good enough!

00:03:57.654 --> 00:03:59.447
I wanted him to record it as Slater.

00:03:59.447 --> 00:04:01.532
What?! You never said that.

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.117
It should've been understood.

00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:04.827
Don't test me, Starling.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.621
A census taker did that once,

00:04:06.621 --> 00:04:09.040
and I ate his liver with dry Cheerios

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.042
and a mashed-up banana.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.463
Sorry, I'm just a little nervous.

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:17.173
When I was a girl,

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.591
I went to live on my uncle's farm,

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:21.803
and I heard these lambs screaming,

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:23.554
screaming as they were being slaughtered.

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:25.473
It was horrible.

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:28.268
And I want to thank
Alan Weiss at William Morris.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:31.271
Also, my high school drama teacher,
Lucas Wohl.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:33.982
Oh, they were just
killing those poor lambs.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:35.316
I wanted to save them, but I couldn't.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.194
And, Mandy and Jenny
at home, go to bed, kids.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:39.821
Mommy did it!

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:42.073
I am coming home with one of these!

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:53.501
CVS brand lotion?

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:56.170
It's the same ingredients as Nivea.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:05:00.133
It puts the off-brand lotion on its skin,

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.844
or else it gets the hose again.

00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:04.595
The top isn't even a pump.

00:05:04.679 --> 00:05:06.848
You're paying for the pump!

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.857
Dr. Lecter, we are running out of time.

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.775
I need you to give me some clue,

00:05:17.859 --> 00:05:20.194
anything that might
lead me in the right direction.

00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:23.239
His name's Buffalo Bill,
heavyset blond kid

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.742
who lives in that crappy place
behind McDonald's.

00:05:25.742 --> 00:05:27.160
Hmm.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.453
I'll have to really lean

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:30.455
on my budding criminology skills

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:33.082
to decipher these obscure breadcrumbs.

00:06:12.163 --> 00:06:13.748
Coming up, dinner.

00:06:13.748 --> 00:06:16.626
But first, I turn my back
to a dangerous murderer.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.391
{\an8}Oh, hey, Sarge.
Your wife called and said it was urgent.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.226
{\an8}Oh, uh, okay.

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:35.937
Yeah, she sounded very not happy.

00:06:35.937 --> 00:06:37.605
You need to call her back ASAP.

00:06:37.605 --> 00:06:38.815
Got it, thanks.

00:06:38.815 --> 00:06:41.651
Starting to think I did this guy a favor.

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:51.494
It puts its finger on the doorbell.

00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:53.037
We're looking for someone.

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:54.497
Have you seen her?

00:06:54.497 --> 00:06:58.626
Oh, wait, is she that
great, big, huge, plump,

00:06:58.626 --> 00:07:02.004
very large, Rubenesque,
fat girl who went missing?

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.506
Yes, she is rather heavy,

00:07:03.506 --> 00:07:05.883
and as you can see,
not particularly attractive.

00:07:05.967 --> 00:07:07.718
We've had reports that her personality

00:07:07.802 --> 00:07:09.262
is quite grating as well.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.472
I can still hear you guys!

00:07:31.492 --> 00:07:33.828
I'm not loving this night vision setting.

00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:37.790
Maybe I should
try <i>Night at the Roxbury</i> vision.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:46.257
- You? Me? You?
- <i>What is love?  </i>
- Aah!

00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:51.554
It puts the bullet in the fat guy.

00:07:55.558 --> 00:07:58.060
And, for having successfully
scaled a cargo net

00:07:58.144 --> 00:08:01.522
and connecting two note cards
with a piece of red string,

00:08:01.606 --> 00:08:06.152
Clarice Starling,
you are now officially a lady FBI.

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:17.538
You should probably answer that.

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:20.082
I mean, you're the closest thing
to a secretary in here.

00:08:21.083 --> 00:08:22.793
Ugh.

00:08:22.877 --> 00:08:26.339
Hello, FBI. This is Clarice speaking.

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:27.882
Hello, Clarice.

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:30.468
I just wanted to let you know
that I respect you,

00:08:30.468 --> 00:08:32.929
and how important it is
that you're a woman.

00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:35.181
Thank you for saying so, Doctor.

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:36.516
'Cause if you were a man,

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:38.768
I would definitely
be captured or dead by now.

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:41.312
- Oh, I...
- Like, if you're Clint Eastwood, I'm dead.

00:08:41.312 --> 00:08:44.023
- Harrison Ford? Dead.
- Well, Doctor, I've really got...

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.234
You know, I'm not betting
against the <i>Twin Peaks</i> guy--

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:47.777
what's his name? Creepy white guy.

00:08:47.777 --> 00:08:50.279
- Kyle MacLachlan.
- Kyle MacLachlan, right.

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:51.531
How do I keep forgetting that?

00:08:51.531 --> 00:08:53.866
It's like in my top five dude names.
I have a list.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.494
- Dr. Lecter, I really have to go.
- So do I.

00:09:00.248 --> 00:09:03.084
I'm having an old friend for dinner.

00:09:03.084 --> 00:09:04.919
Y-You're gonna eat a friend?

00:09:04.919 --> 00:09:06.504
That was kind of
supposed to be the last line,

00:09:06.504 --> 00:09:07.755
and you ruined it.

00:09:07.755 --> 00:09:09.674
I'm gonna say it again
and then hang up quickly.

00:09:10.967 --> 00:09:13.135
I'm having an old friend for dinner.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.178
<i>What?!</i>

00:09:14.262 --> 00:09:16.055
Oh, my God, this bitch.

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:23.854
<i>My name is...</i>

00:09:23.938 --> 00:09:26.649
<i>whatever Kevin Spacey's name was
in this movie.</i>

00:09:26.649 --> 00:09:28.526
<i>I bet you think behind that door is</i>

00:09:28.526 --> 00:09:30.152
<i>a happy, all-American family.</i>

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:31.153
<i>Nope.</i>

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:32.530
<i>Just me in the shower</i>

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.532
<i>with Johnson & Johnson and Johnson.</i>

00:09:34.532 --> 00:09:36.742
<i>There were some tears.</i>

00:09:36.826 --> 00:09:39.078
<i>That's my wife out there, cutting roses.</i>

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:41.831
<i>Oh, just a heads-up,
there's a ton of roses in this.</i>

00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:44.375
<i>I guess they're
supposed to mean something. (sighs)</i>

00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:45.793
<i>You know, when I agreed to this,</i>

00:09:45.793 --> 00:09:48.004
<i>I 100% thought it was</i> American Pie.

00:09:48.004 --> 00:09:50.089
<i>Always read the second word of the title</i>

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:51.424
<i>before you sign something.</i>

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:54.218
Oh, hi, Carolyn. We're your gay neighbors.

00:09:54.302 --> 00:09:56.137
That's right, and we're
the only happy people

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:57.638
in the entire film.

00:09:57.722 --> 00:09:58.889
<i>Oh, that's the other thing.</i>

00:09:58.973 --> 00:10:00.558
<i>This movie really wants you to know</i>

00:10:00.558 --> 00:10:03.185
<i>that traditional families
are the messed-up ones.</i>

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:04.687
<i>If you don't want two hours of that,</i>

00:10:04.687 --> 00:10:06.272
<i>go turn on</i> The Matrix.

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:07.857
<i>Aw, why aren't we doing that?</i>

00:10:07.857 --> 00:10:09.191
Have a great day,

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.485
two-dimensional '90s gay neighbors.

00:10:11.569 --> 00:10:14.864
- Who are both named Jim.
- Right, who are both named Jim.

00:10:15.948 --> 00:10:18.534
- Good morning, my darling.
- Hello, my love.

00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:20.870
<i>Keep in mind
that 9/11 hasn't happened yet.</i>

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.955
<i>So a strained family dynamic</i>

00:10:23.039 --> 00:10:25.166
<i>is still the most dramatic thing there is.</i>

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.878
Wow, what a beautiful,
fully heterosexual neighborhood.

00:10:28.878 --> 00:10:31.797
Yeah, no. What's up is down here, bro.

00:10:31.881 --> 00:10:34.258
Oh, hi, you must be our new neighbors.

00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:36.093
I'm Carolyn Burnham,

00:10:36.177 --> 00:10:39.055
RE/MAX's top crying realtor in the area.

00:10:39.055 --> 00:10:40.973
Uh, thanks, but we just bought a house,

00:10:41.057 --> 00:10:42.808
so we don't really need a realtor.

00:10:45.603 --> 00:10:47.688
- You don't?
- S-Sorry.

00:10:47.772 --> 00:10:49.523
It's okay. You know what?

00:10:49.607 --> 00:10:50.816
We'll buy another one.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.152
Oh, great. Great.

00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:55.780
Oh, looks like your son and my daughter

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.281
are getting to know each other.

00:10:57.365 --> 00:11:00.576
Check out this video
I took of a plastic bag.

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:05.831
I'm thinking about sending it in

00:11:05.915 --> 00:11:08.042
to <i>America's Funniest Home Videos.</i>

00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:10.127
Really? Do you think it's funny enough?

00:11:10.211 --> 00:11:13.130
I don't know. I just want to spend $2,000

00:11:13.214 --> 00:11:16.842
flying to Los Angeles to maybe win $1,000.

00:11:21.097 --> 00:11:23.140
<i>That's halftime.</i>

00:11:23.224 --> 00:11:25.351
<i>And now, please welcome
the Suburbia High School</i>

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:28.354
<i>cheer quad, the Dockers Zipper Pushers.</i>

00:11:40.825 --> 00:11:42.827
Who is that?

00:11:56.424 --> 00:11:58.259
Aah! Aw, damn it. Aw, stop. Stop.

00:11:58.259 --> 00:12:01.262
I have seasonal allergies, guys.

00:12:01.262 --> 00:12:03.514
<i>All right.</i>

00:12:03.514 --> 00:12:04.807
<i>Now the marching band to play</i>

00:12:04.807 --> 00:12:07.017
<i>the Suburbia High School fight song.</i>

00:12:12.106 --> 00:12:13.733
Geez, again with this song?

00:12:13.733 --> 00:12:16.152
Shut up and kiss me, other gay Jim.

00:12:18.529 --> 00:12:21.365
Oh, no. No.

00:12:21.449 --> 00:12:23.325
I'm very against that.

00:12:23.409 --> 00:12:25.286
Remember that for later.

00:12:25.286 --> 00:12:27.037
<i>The next day, I quit my job</i>

00:12:27.121 --> 00:12:29.373
<i>and was in no way run out of the industry</i>

00:12:29.457 --> 00:12:31.083
<i>for groping a busboy in Nantucket.</i>

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:33.169
It was a joke. I was razzing the guy.

00:12:33.169 --> 00:12:34.462
Come on.

00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:39.759
<i>I got a new job
at a fake movie fast food restaurant.</i>

00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:43.179
<i>God, why are movies
so bad at naming restaurants?</i>

00:12:43.179 --> 00:12:46.265
Welcome to
Mr. Smiley's BurgerTownVilleLand.

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:48.309
Would you like to try a Large McIntyre?

00:12:48.309 --> 00:12:51.645
<i>Yes, my lover and I
will each have adultery burgers.</i>

00:12:51.729 --> 00:12:53.606
Second window.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:59.612
- Two adultery burgers.
- Lester!

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:02.281
Listen, let's not make a big scene here.

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.699
We can talk about this when we get...

00:13:03.783 --> 00:13:08.537
<i>You</i> don't get to tell <i>me</i>
what to do anymore.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.499
We need more ketchup.

00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:14.585
All right, there are some things
you can tell me to do.

00:13:14.585 --> 00:13:17.129
<i>After that, I started
lifting weights in my garage.</i>

00:13:17.213 --> 00:13:18.714
<i>But I lost track of a spider</i>

00:13:18.798 --> 00:13:20.341
<i>that crawled behind the heavy ones,</i>

00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:23.052
<i>so I had to use the dainty weights
ladies walk with.</i>

00:13:23.052 --> 00:13:24.804
Oh, hey. You got those drugs?

00:13:24.804 --> 00:13:26.180
Yep, right here.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.890
Oh, my God.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.309
Look at that plastic bag.

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:32.353
So beautiful.

00:13:32.353 --> 00:13:34.688
Do you do a lot of the drugs yourself?

00:13:34.772 --> 00:13:36.023
I do, yes.

00:13:36.023 --> 00:13:38.234
Okay, let me just get on my knees

00:13:38.234 --> 00:13:42.029
and roll a joint at crotch level
like all drug dealers do.

00:13:42.029 --> 00:13:44.365
Great, and I'll just lean back,
away from the drugs

00:13:44.365 --> 00:13:46.617
like all drug users do.

00:13:49.036 --> 00:13:50.830
What the hell?

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:52.289
Am I seeing what I think I'm seeing?

00:13:52.373 --> 00:13:53.958
Help me out here, Mr. Furley.

00:13:53.958 --> 00:13:56.210
How did this thing win an Oscar?

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.712
It's basically <i>Austin Powers.</i>

00:14:01.799 --> 00:14:03.759
Yo, yo, check this out.

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:06.512
What if, like, Kramer is just

00:14:06.512 --> 00:14:09.056
a figment of Jerry's imagination?

00:14:09.056 --> 00:14:12.476
- Wow. Yeah.
-'Cause think about it.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:16.856
We-we never see him
interacting with anyone else.

00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:18.399
Yeah.

00:14:18.399 --> 00:14:22.361
Well-well, wait.
I mean, w... Uh, we-we do.

00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:25.322
Oh, boy, am I glad you're here.

00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:28.325
I don't think I like what I saw earlier.

00:14:28.409 --> 00:14:29.702
Oh, was it <i>The Phantom Menace,</i>

00:14:29.702 --> 00:14:31.412
which also came out this same year?

00:14:31.412 --> 00:14:32.663
Yeah, what a mess.

00:14:32.663 --> 00:14:35.666
Ricky, go on home.
I need to talk to Lester.

00:14:35.666 --> 00:14:37.543
Aw, I don't want to.

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:39.837
: There's plastic bags.

00:14:39.837 --> 00:14:41.714
There are?

00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:46.343
Hey, you know how
there's two things we know for sure?

00:14:46.427 --> 00:14:49.179
We'll always be able
to bring box cutters on planes,

00:14:49.263 --> 00:14:51.807
- and I'm heterosexual?
- Yeah, of course.

00:14:51.891 --> 00:14:54.977
Well, turns out only
one of those things is true.

00:14:54.977 --> 00:14:56.896
Mm...

00:14:56.896 --> 00:14:59.023
Look, I think I gave you the wrong idea

00:14:59.023 --> 00:15:02.026
with these pink weights
and pantomiming oral with your son.

00:15:02.026 --> 00:15:04.278
- I'm straight.
- I'm so sorry!

00:15:04.278 --> 00:15:06.906
I got to go start a megachurch!

00:15:06.906 --> 00:15:08.657
Eh, seems right.

00:15:10.534 --> 00:15:12.828
Oh, hey, what are you doing here?

00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:14.121
I have a flight tomorrow,

00:15:14.121 --> 00:15:16.624
and Jane said
I could borrow your box cutter.

00:15:16.624 --> 00:15:19.209
Man, I love cutting boxes on planes.

00:15:19.293 --> 00:15:23.172
And also-- and this is kind
of embarrassing and unearned--

00:15:23.172 --> 00:15:25.507
but I think you're sexy,

00:15:25.591 --> 00:15:27.676
and I want to have sex with you.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.637
Ah, sweet! Let's do this.

00:15:29.637 --> 00:15:32.890
I should let you know, I'm a virgin.

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.350
Not a deal-breaker.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.976
And I should let you know

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:38.437
I'm Chris Hansen from <i>To Catch a Predator.</i>

00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:40.105
Aw, crap. Somebody shoot me.

00:15:44.151 --> 00:15:45.444
Sorry, I didn't mean to...

00:15:45.444 --> 00:15:47.529
Whoa, you're Chris Hansen!

00:15:47.613 --> 00:15:50.866
Hey, what do you do
with all the leftover pedophile pizza?

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:53.035
<i>Well, that was</i> American Beauty.

00:15:53.035 --> 00:15:54.662
<i>See you at the Oscars.</i>

00:15:54.662 --> 00:15:56.205
<i>I'll be there with my mom.</i>

00:15:56.205 --> 00:15:58.791
<i>That's not a big,
obvious sign of something, right?</i>

00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:15.849
- How's work, Ralph?
- It's a breeze.

00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:20.270
- Give my best to Judy.
- Will do.

00:16:26.652 --> 00:16:29.446
Hi, my name's Forrest.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:30.906
Forrest Gump.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.367
Would it be okay
if I sugarcoat race relations

00:16:33.367 --> 00:16:36.078
in the South for the next
two and a half hours?

00:16:36.078 --> 00:16:39.331
Honey, I'm a Black woman
in a '90s Hollywood movie,

00:16:39.415 --> 00:16:41.667
- that's what I'm here for.
- Great.

00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:45.337
My mama always said life
was like a box of Good & Plenty:

00:16:45.421 --> 00:16:47.798
most people just throw it away.

00:16:47.798 --> 00:16:50.175
<i>One day on the bus to school,</i>

00:16:50.259 --> 00:16:52.052
<i>I met Jenny.</i>

00:16:52.136 --> 00:16:54.471
<i>She was the love of my life.</i>

00:16:56.515 --> 00:16:59.143
Hey, look, it's a guy
with nonstandard legs.

00:16:59.143 --> 00:17:01.937
Let's bully and throw
rocks at him and not me.

00:17:03.022 --> 00:17:05.399
Run, Forrest, run!

00:17:06.358 --> 00:17:07.985
<i>And in a magical moment</i>

00:17:07.985 --> 00:17:10.738
<i>whose explanation
I assume was cut for time,</i>

00:17:10.738 --> 00:17:13.824
<i>I could suddenly run very fast.</i>

00:17:13.824 --> 00:17:15.409
<i>But I happened to do it</i>

00:17:15.409 --> 00:17:18.287
<i>in front of the meanest
lifeguard in Alabama.</i>

00:17:18.287 --> 00:17:21.874
- No running!
- It's for a movie. God.

00:17:21.874 --> 00:17:23.667
<i>I was such a fast runner,</i>

00:17:23.751 --> 00:17:26.712
<i>I went on to play college movie football,</i>

00:17:26.712 --> 00:17:30.591
<i>where all the tacklers
dive two feet behind you and miss.</i>

00:17:32.801 --> 00:17:34.511
After I graduated,

00:17:34.595 --> 00:17:37.389
I joined the Army
and got shipped off to war.

00:17:37.473 --> 00:17:41.143
<i>Vietnam is where
I met my best friend, Bubba,</i>

00:17:41.143 --> 00:17:44.480
<i>who really wanted
to have his own squid fishing boat.</i>

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.940
<i>In fact, he knew just about</i>

00:17:47.024 --> 00:17:48.901
<i>everything you could do with a squid.</i>

00:17:48.901 --> 00:17:51.236
Well, there's calamari...

00:17:53.322 --> 00:17:55.032
That's about it.

00:17:55.032 --> 00:17:57.576
Ambush!

00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:01.163
Oh, my God, Lieutenant Dan!

00:18:02.748 --> 00:18:05.167
Damn it, save yourself, Gump.

00:18:05.167 --> 00:18:07.878
- Leave me here.
- All right.

00:18:09.046 --> 00:18:11.048
<i>Bubba was also shot.</i>

00:18:11.048 --> 00:18:13.842
<i>And as always happens when a soldier dies,</i>

00:18:13.926 --> 00:18:16.011
<i>we discussed business ideas.</i>

00:18:16.095 --> 00:18:19.264
I'm dying, Forrest.

00:18:19.348 --> 00:18:21.975
I want you to buy
a squid boat in my honor.

00:18:22.059 --> 00:18:25.187
How about a gym
exclusively for big white women?

00:18:25.187 --> 00:18:28.982
- There could be machines that...
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:18:29.066 --> 00:18:32.277
You had me at "big white women."

00:18:34.196 --> 00:18:36.740
<i>After I got home from Vietnam,</i>

00:18:36.824 --> 00:18:39.535
<i>I got to speak at a generic protest.</i>

00:18:39.535 --> 00:18:42.746
There's only one thing
to say about Vietnam:

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.916
I had this awesome red stuff
on all my food.

00:18:45.916 --> 00:18:47.668
I don't 'member what it's called.

00:18:47.668 --> 00:18:50.254
It's not hot sauce, but it's not ketchup.

00:18:50.254 --> 00:18:52.714
I think it's got a rooster on the label.

00:18:52.798 --> 00:18:54.133
Forrest!

00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:57.553
Jenny!

00:18:58.637 --> 00:18:59.972
Aah! Son of a bitch!

00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:03.350
See, guys? This is why no running.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.602
<i>And then--
I know, it's still not over yet--</i>

00:19:05.686 --> 00:19:08.021
<i>I bought a squid boat.</i>

00:19:08.105 --> 00:19:10.399
<i>Lieutenant Dan was also working with me.</i>

00:19:10.399 --> 00:19:12.609
<i>And you know who's super helpful on a boat</i>

00:19:12.693 --> 00:19:14.736
<i>that's constantly rocking in the water?</i>

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:16.196
<i>A wheelchair guy.</i>

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.448
Hey, Forrest, I got our lunches.

00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:21.618
Aah!

00:19:24.454 --> 00:19:26.498
So after I was rich,

00:19:26.582 --> 00:19:29.710
Jenny came back
and had sex with me one time.

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:32.212
Wow, that was great.

00:19:32.296 --> 00:19:35.007
Sorry I was naming presidents during.

00:19:35.007 --> 00:19:36.758
So, we getting married or what?

00:19:36.842 --> 00:19:39.344
You don't want to marry me, Forrest.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:41.930
Yeah, you're right.

00:19:42.014 --> 00:19:44.183
Okay, well, have a good night.

00:19:44.183 --> 00:19:46.685
<i>And then, shockingly late in the movie,</i>

00:19:46.685 --> 00:19:48.687
<i>I started running again.</i>

00:19:48.687 --> 00:19:50.772
<i>Like, across the country.</i>

00:19:50.856 --> 00:19:52.107
<i>Several times.</i>

00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:53.859
<i>The whole sequence
is a full eight minutes.</i>

00:19:53.859 --> 00:19:55.861
<i>I mean, sometimes this whole movie
feels like it was written</i>

00:19:55.861 --> 00:19:58.113
<i>by a seven-year-old
who just ate a bunch of candy.</i>

00:19:58.197 --> 00:20:00.240
<i>But I checked, it's just a regular guy.</i>

00:20:00.324 --> 00:20:02.034
<i>Anyway, at least we were finally</i>

00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:04.369
<i>to the time in our nation's history</i>

00:20:04.453 --> 00:20:05.746
<i>when I could listen to this.</i>

00:20:05.746 --> 00:20:09.166
<i>Princes, princes who adore you.  </i>

00:20:14.588 --> 00:20:15.714
Forrest!

00:20:15.714 --> 00:20:19.051
I brought you chocolates
picked over by strangers.

00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:20.886
Forrest, I'm sick.

00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:23.722
Sick? With what?

00:20:23.722 --> 00:20:26.016
Oh, I did a movie about that once.

00:20:26.016 --> 00:20:27.643
It's called <i>Splash.</i>

00:20:27.643 --> 00:20:30.562
No, Forrest.

00:20:30.646 --> 00:20:33.357
Oh, I thought you said mermaids.

00:20:33.357 --> 00:20:35.817
But I did a movie about your thing, too.

00:20:35.901 --> 00:20:37.486
But that's not all.

00:20:37.486 --> 00:20:39.112
I want you to meet my son.

00:20:39.196 --> 00:20:41.698
Six hours in makeup. One line.

00:20:41.782 --> 00:20:43.283
You're his father.

00:20:43.367 --> 00:20:45.285
Father?

00:20:45.369 --> 00:20:47.788
Is he... like me?

00:20:47.788 --> 00:20:49.081
Uhp, you died.

00:20:49.081 --> 00:20:50.749
And... feather!

00:21:34.001 --> 00:21:35.961
